"""KV-P1T-TESTS adapter contract. An adapter is a Python module (given to run_p1t.py by path) that defines the module-
level functions below. Any function may raise NotImplementedError("T<n>: <why>"): the runner then records every case
that needs it as SKIP, and a run with any SKIP is PARTIAL (exit 3), never PASS. A missing function counts as
NotImplementedError. Any other exception from an adapter function is a FAIL of that case (the message is kept).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ T2-T6 (host arrays)
All arrays are NumPy, C-contiguous, float32 in and float32 out. The adapter owns upload and download (and any device
synchronization: the returned array must hold the finished result). Batch is the leading axis; time is the last axis.

  conv1d(x, w, b, *, stride, pads, dilation, groups, weight_storage) -> y
      ONNX Conv, 1-D. x [N, C, T]; w [O, C/groups, K]; b [O] or None; stride, dilation, groups: int;
      pads: (begin, end) zero padding of the time axis. weight_storage: 'fp32' or 'fp16'. 'fp16' means the weight
      tensor w is stored at fp16 (round to nearest even) and the math is fp32 (D6: fp16 storage, fp32 accumulate);
      the bias and the activations stay fp32. y [N, O, (T + pb + pe - dilation*(K-1) - 1)//stride + 1].
  conv_transpose1d(x, w, b, *, stride, pads, output_padding, dilation, groups, weight_storage) -> y
      ONNX ConvTranspose, 1-D. w [C, O/groups, K] (ONNX layout); output length
      stride*(T-1) + output_padding + dilation*(K-1) + 1 - pb - pe. Must be deterministic (no atomics-order
      dependence): the runner checks two calls bitwise.
  lstm(x, W, R, B, *, direction, hidden_size, initial_h, initial_c, layout) -> (Y, Y_h, Y_c)
      ONNX LSTM. layout='onnx' is the only value the runner passes and means: ONNX `layout` attribute 0 (x is
      [T, batch, input]); W [D, 4H, input], R [D, 4H, H], B [D, 8H] = [Wb; Rb]; gate order i, o, f, c (ONNX), NOT
      torch's i, f, g, o; default activations (sigmoid, tanh, tanh), no clip, no peepholes. direction is 'forward',
      'reverse' or 'bidirectional' (D = 2: index 0 forward, index 1 reverse). initial_h / initial_c [D, batch, H].
      Returns Y [T, D, batch, H], Y_h [D, batch, H], Y_c [D, batch, H]. The shipped nodes' sequence_lens equal T
      (or are absent), so the contract carries no sequence_lens; the runner asserts this per case.
  instance_norm1d(x, scale, bias, *, eps) -> y
      ONNX InstanceNormalization on [N, C, T]: per (n, c) mean and biased variance over T; fp32 statistics.
  layer_norm(x, scale, bias, *, axis, eps) -> y
      ONNX LayerNormalization: normalize over axes [axis, rank); bias may be None.
  group_norm(x, scale, bias, *, groups, eps) -> y
      GroupNorm on [N, C, T], per-channel affine (torch.nn.GroupNorm / ONNX GroupNormalization-21).
  upsample_nearest1d(x, *, scale) -> y
      ONNX Resize mode=nearest, coordinate_transformation_mode=asymmetric, nearest_mode=floor (the shipped nodes'
      attributes), scales [1, 1, scale], scale an integer (2 or 300 in Kokoro): y[..., i] = x[..., floor(i / scale)].
      Exact: bitwise equal to the oracle.
  reflection_pad1d(x, *, pads) -> y
      ONNX Pad mode=reflect on the time axis, pads = (begin, end) (Kokoro: (1, 0)). Exact.
  rint(x) -> y
      ONNX Round: round half to even, sign of zero kept (rint(-0.4) = -0.0), +-Inf and NaN pass through. Exact
      (NaN compares equal to NaN whatever its payload, LD9).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ T1 (device tensors)
The adapter's device tensor type must implement the DLPack Python protocol (Python array API data-interchange):
  tensor.__dlpack__(*, stream=None, max_version=None, dl_device=None, copy=None) -> PyCapsule
      Zero-copy export. `stream` is the CONSUMER's stream (DLPack ints: None or 1 = legacy default stream, 2 = per-
      thread default stream, > 2 = a cudaStream_t, -1 = no synchronization). Unless it is -1, the producer must order
      the consumer's stream after all work it has queued on its own stream that touches the tensor (event record +
      cudaStreamWaitEvent, or an equivalent synchronization) before returning. The capsule must keep the memory
      alive after the producer object's last Python reference is dropped.
  tensor.__dlpack_device__() -> (2, ordinal)          # kDLCUDA = 2
and the module must define:
  t1_from_dlpack(obj) -> tensor        zero-copy import of any DLPack producer; the result aliases obj's memory,
                                       keeps obj's owner alive after the caller drops obj, and is ordered after the
                                       producer's pending work (the adapter asks obj.__dlpack__(stream=<its own
                                       stream as a DLPack int>), so the producer synchronizes).
  t1_empty(shape, dtype) -> tensor     allocate on the adapter's stream; dtype 'float32' or 'float16'.
  t1_fill(tensor, value)               write `value` everywhere, queued on the adapter's stream (may be asynchronous).
  t1_read(tensor) -> np.ndarray        synchronize the adapter's stream ONLY (not the device), then copy to host.
  t1_data_ptr(tensor) -> int           device address of element 0.
  t1_stream() -> int                   the adapter's CUDA stream handle (0 = legacy default stream; TensorCUDA's
                                       only stream).
The runner's T1 tests use torch (CUDA) as the external peer. They check pointer identity and write-through both ways
(zero-copy), the device tuple, owner lifetime after the producer's last reference is dropped (with same-size
allocations made to reuse freed memory), and stream ordering both ways (the producer queues a long
`torch.cuda._sleep` then a write on its stream; the consumer reads on another stream). Lifetime and stream tests run
knobs.T1_TRIALS trials and report the failure count: a race may not reproduce on every trial.

Prior art: the Python array API standard's data-interchange protocol (`__dlpack__(stream=)`, `__dlpack_device__`,
Consortium for Python Data API Standards, 2020-2023) and DLPack (dmlc/dlpack, 2017-); the CUDA Array Interface v3
stream semantics (Numba, 2020); the event-record + stream-wait fence is the standard CUDA cross-stream idiom. ONNX
operator specs for every T2-T6 signature. Ours: the split into host-array functions plus a device sub-contract.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import inspect

HOST_FUNCTIONS = {
    'conv1d': ('x', 'w', 'b', 'stride', 'pads', 'dilation', 'groups', 'weight_storage'),
    'conv_transpose1d': ('x', 'w', 'b', 'stride', 'pads', 'output_padding', 'dilation', 'groups', 'weight_storage'),
    'lstm': ('x', 'W', 'R', 'B', 'direction', 'hidden_size', 'initial_h', 'initial_c', 'layout'),
    'instance_norm1d': ('x', 'scale', 'bias', 'eps'),
    'layer_norm': ('x', 'scale', 'bias', 'axis', 'eps'),
    'group_norm': ('x', 'scale', 'bias', 'groups', 'eps'),
    'upsample_nearest1d': ('x', 'scale'),
    'reflection_pad1d': ('x', 'pads'),
    'rint': ('x',),
}
T1_FUNCTIONS = ('t1_from_dlpack', 't1_empty', 't1_fill', 't1_read', 't1_data_ptr', 't1_stream')
ITEM_FUNCTIONS = {
    'T1': T1_FUNCTIONS,
    'T2': ('conv1d',),
    'T3': ('conv_transpose1d',),
    'T4': ('lstm',),
    'T5': ('instance_norm1d', 'layer_norm', 'group_norm'),
    'T6': ('upsample_nearest1d', 'reflection_pad1d', 'rint'),
}
WEIGHT_STORAGES = ('fp32', 'fp16')
LSTM_LAYOUT = 'onnx'


def signature_report(module) -> dict:
    """For every contract function: present / missing, and whether its parameter names match the contract."""
    out = {}
    for name, params in HOST_FUNCTIONS.items():
        fn = getattr(module, name, None)
        if fn is None:
            out[name] = {'present': False}
            continue
        try:
            got = tuple(inspect.signature(fn).parameters)
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            got = None
        out[name] = {'present': True, 'params_match': got == params, 'params': list(got) if got else None}
    for name in T1_FUNCTIONS:
        out[name] = {'present': getattr(module, name, None) is not None}
    return out


def get(module, name):
    """The adapter's function, or a stand-in that raises NotImplementedError (a missing function is a SKIP)."""
    fn = getattr(module, name, None)
    if fn is None:
        def missing(*a, **k):
            raise NotImplementedError(f'adapter defines no {name}()')
        return missing
    return fn

