     1	// tc_signal LSTM (P1T-M3, T4): ONNX LSTM semantics, fp32, deterministic, no atomics, no fast-math.
     2	//
     3	// Semantics (ONNX LSTM operator, layout 0, default activations Sigmoid/Tanh/Tanh, no clip, no peepholes,
     4	// input_forget 0): x [T, N, I]; W [D, 4H, I]; R [D, 4H, H]; B [D, 8H] = [Wb; Rb]; gate blocks along 4H in the ONNX order
     5	// i, o, f, c (NOT torch's i, f, g, o). Per direction slot d and step:
     6	//     z  = (x_t . W[d]^T + Wb[d]) + h_{t-1} . R[d]^T + Rb[d]
     7	//     i  = sigmoid(z_i), o = sigmoid(z_o), f = sigmoid(z_f), c~ = tanh(z_c)
     8	//     c  = f * c_{t-1} + i * c~,  h = o * tanh(c)
     9	// D = 2 (bidirectional): slot 0 runs forward, slot 1 runs in reverse; a reverse slot at loop step s reads time
    10	// T-1-s and writes Y[T-1-s, d]. Y_h / Y_c are the state after each slot's last step.
    11	//
    12	// Structure (Project-Voice TENSOR_IMPL_PLAN_P1T.md §5 T4; LD51 amendment A2; order P1T-M3 "Structure"):
    13	//  1. initial state -> Y_h / Y_c (D2D copy or zero), on the legacy stream;
    14	//  2. one cublasSgemm per direction for the input projection of ALL steps: G_x[d] = X[T*N, I] . W[d]^T, accumulated
    15	//     onto G_x pre-filled with Wb[d] (beta = 1; beta = 0 without B);
    16	//  3. a host C++ loop over the T steps (inside the one _tc_signal call; no Python per step, no per-step DLPack):
    17	//     one cublasSgemmStridedBatched over the D slots, G_h[d] = h_{t-1}[d] . R[d]^T (h = Y_h), then one fused cell
    18	//     kernel (adds Rb, activations, c/h update, writes Y_c, Y_h and Y).
    19	//
    20	// Numerics contract (TENSOR_IMPL_PLAN_P1T.md §4):
    21	//  * fp32 everywhere; cuBLAS in CUBLAS_DEFAULT_MATH (never TF32), atomics not allowed, pointer mode host;
    22	//  * transcendentals are the CUDA math library's accurate expf() and tanhf() (documented max error 2 ulp each); none of
    23	//    the double-underscore fast intrinsics (exp, tanh, divide) and no fast-math compiler flag (CMakeLists.txt refuses it
    24	//    for the whole package);
    25	//  * every element of every kernel is written by exactly one thread with a fixed operation order, and cuBLAS runs with
    26	//    atomics not allowed on one stream, so two calls on the same inputs are bitwise equal. No atomic adds anywhere.
    27	//
    28	// Prior art:
    29	//  * LSTM: Hochreiter & Schmidhuber, "Long Short-Term Memory" (1997); the forget gate: Gers, Schmidhuber & Cummins,
    30	//    "Learning to Forget: Continual Prediction with LSTM" (2000). Taken: the cell equations.
    31	//  * ONNX LSTM operator specification (onnx/docs/Operators.md, LSTM): gate order i,o,f,c, B = [Wb; Rb], the Y / Y_h /
    32	//    Y_c layouts, the reverse direction. Taken: the semantics, verbatim.
    33	//  * Input projection hoisted out of the recurrence as one large GEMM over all time steps, leaving only the h . R^T
    34	//    product inside the step loop: Appleyard, Kocisky & Blunsom, "Optimizing Performance of Recurrent Neural Networks
    35	//    on GPUs" (2016), the design cuDNN's RNN API uses. Taken: that split. Ours: the plain correctness-first form (one
    36	//    strided-batched GEMM + one fused cell kernel per step, host loop), with no persistent kernel and no stream overlap.
    37	//  * Numerically stable logistic sigmoid by splitting on the sign of z (evaluate exp of a non-positive argument only):
    38	//    standard practice (e.g. the log-sum-exp / softplus folklore; no single source known to me). Taken: the split.
    39	//  * Row-major GEMM through column-major BLAS by computing C^T = B^T A^T: standard BLAS practice (no single source).
    40	// The recurrent state kept in the Y_h / Y_c outputs (no separate state scratch) is ours; no prior art known to me.
    41	#include "lstm_ops.h"
